## This code block defines a DAX query that retrieves tax rate data from a Power BI semantic model using OLE DB connections. 
## The query selects specific columns from the 'Tax' table, including Country, Country Key, Year, ETR (Effective Tax Rate), and CTR (Corporate Tax Rate).
## The results are ordered by Country and Year in ascending order.
## Note that the connection string has been specifically excluded from this file for security reasons, and the query is intended to be executed within the context of a secure Power BI environment where the user has appropriate access permissions.
## Downstream this query is used to support the post tax metrics derivation in the scenario model engine, which calculates post-tax financial metrics based on the retrieved tax rates for different countries and years.

EVALUATE
  SELECTCOLUMNS(
    'Tax',
    "Country", 'Tax'[Country],
    "Country Key", 'Tax'[Country Key],
    "Year", 'Tax'[Year],
    "ETR", 'Tax'[ETR],
    "CTR", 'Tax'[CTR]
  )
ORDER BY
  [Country] ASC,
  [Year] ASC